## Service status

| Reviewer | Status | |
|---|---|---|
| **Claude** | ⚪ Too few findings | 33% of 3 findings addressed |
| **Greptile** | ⚪ Too few findings | 0% of 2 findings addressed |

_🟢 Good service: at least 60% of findings addressed. 🟡 Minor delays: 40–59%. 🔴 Severe delays: under 40%. ⚪ Fewer than 5 findings: no status._

## By reviewer

| Reviewer | PRs | Findings | Addressed | Dismissed | Ignored | Not addressed | Outdated | Per PR | First comment |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Claude | 2 | 3 (2 inline, 1 summary) | 1 (33%) | 1 (33%) | 0 (0%) | 1 (33%) | 0 | 1.5 | 2m |
| Greptile | 2 | 2 | 0 (0%) | 0 (0%) | 2 (100%) | 0 (0%) | 0 | 1.0 | 10m |

_**Addressed**: code near the comment changed afterwards, or a reply/👍 confirmed it. **Dismissed**: 👎, a dismissing reply, or resolved with no nearby change. **Ignored**: no response. **Not addressed**: a summary-comment item with no nearby change (summaries have no replies or resolution, so dismissed and ignored look the same). **Outdated**: GitHub marked the thread outdated but no nearby change was found. **Per PR**: findings per PR the reviewer commented on. **First comment**: median time from PR opened to the review being delivered._

